KeywordAbility(
    name: "squad",
    params: [Cost],
    spelling: "squad <Param(0)>",
    grammar: FixedKeyword(
        surface: "squad",
    ),
    // STOP. "Squad [cost]" means "As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay
    // [cost] ANY NUMBER OF TIMES" and "When this creature enters, if its squad cost was
    // paid, create a token that's a copy of it for each time its squad cost was paid."
    // [CR#702.157a] `StaticSpec::AddedCost` carries a cost and an `offered` flag and no
    // repetition count, so "any number of times" cannot be written (the cause Replicate
    // shares). Its second ability is writable and pinned
    // (`Proofs/KeywordDefinitionRegimes.lean`, `okSquadSecondAbility`):
    // `triggeredIf(enters(thisCreature), keywordCostPaid(squad, thisCreature),
    // create(timesPaid(ByKeyword(squad), thisCreature), copyOf(thisCreature)))`. The
    // definition is not declared without its first ability, since a declared
    // definition is every ability the keyword represents [CR#702.157a].
)
